<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kullaba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kullaba was one of the two original settlements that grew together to form the Sumerian city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> in the 4th millennium BCE, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eanna">Eanna</a>. It contained the sanctuary of the sky god An, with the White Temple on its high terrace. In Sumerian poetry Kullaba is used as a name for Uruk itself, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgamesh">Gilgamesh</a> is called lord of Kullaba.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kullaba.jpg" alt="Kullaba" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lamassu Design Gurdjieff · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anu_district.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
